===Etymology 1===
From {{bor|en|he|-}} {{he-m|חומר|dwv=חֹמֶר|tr=khómer|gloss=[[clay]], [[heap]], [[large]] [[unit]] of [[volume]]}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{l|en|chomer}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|historical|_|units of measure}} A [[former]] [[Hebrew]] [[unit]] of [[dry]] [[volume]], [[about]] [[equal]] to 230{{nbsp}}[[L]] or {{frac|6|1|2}}{{nbsp}}US{{nbsp}}[[bushel]]s.
#* {{RQ:KJV Ezekiel|45|11|passage=The [[ephah]] and the [[bath]] shall be of one measure, that the [[bath]] may contain the tenth part of an homer, and the [[ephah]] the tenth part of an '''homer''': the measure thereof shall be after the '''homer'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1922|author=James Joyce|title=Ulysses|passage=Head up! For every newbegotten thou shalt gather thy '''homer''' of ripe wheat.}}
# {{lb|en|historical|_|units of measure}} {{syn of|en|cor|nodot=a}}: [[approximately]] the [[same]] [[volume]] as a [[liquid]] [[measure]].
#* {{RQ:KJV Ezekiel|45|11|passage=The [[ephah]] and the [[bath]] shall be of one measure, that the [[bath]] may contain the tenth part of an '''homer''', and the [[ephah]] the tenth part of an homer: the measure thereof shall be after the '''homer'''.}}

=====Usage notes=====
In English, sometimes confounded with the much smaller {{m|en|omer}}.

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|en|cor}}, {{l|en|kor}}

